<!--
  O+O 200 GeV with initial-state radiation and jet energy loss, one MUSIC run per event (no
  two-stage hydro).  Driven by run_prod_oo_isr.py in this folder.

  OO_MCGlauber_MUSIC_isr_rhictune.xml: this file with the Pythia settings of the RHIC p+p 200
  GeV hard tune (analysis/OO-RHIC, 2026-11-22) in <Hard><PythiaGun><LinesToRead>, so that O+O
  and its p+p reference (analysis/OO-RHIC, run "oo_ref": alpha_s 0.152, C_v 0.25, Q0 2) run
  the same chain.  OO_MCGlauber_MUSIC_isr.xml (the driver's default) has only HardQCD:all =
  on, i.e. Pythia's defaults: alpha_s 0.130, PDF:pSet 13 (iMATTER uses NNPDF3.1 NNLO) and
  Pythia's soft MPI (pTmin 0.2: ~3.7 MPI per event besides the hard one, each subtracted
  from the hard nucleon pair).  Pass it with the driver option user-xml.

    IS (3dMCGlauber, O16, positions only)
      -> Hard: PythiaIsrGun -> iMATTER (ISR, 0 -> -maxT) -> 3dMCGlauber strings from what
               the hard scattering left (MCGlauberGenString)
      -> NullPreDynamics -> MUSIC (music4gpu)            the medium, from those strings
      -> Eloss: Matter + LBT in MUSIC's medium, from -maxT   the final-state shower
      -> JetHadronization: iColored                      final partons + beam remnants,
                                                         through the colour flow
      (-> SoftParticlization: iSS                        with option bulk-hadrons N)

  X-SCAPE builds this chain from <Hard><ISR> (JetScape::DetermineTaskListFromXML, branch
  oo_isr_test).  The order of the blocks matters: <IS> before <Hard>.

  The MUSIC settings are the tuned O+O set of X-SCAPE's config/BulkFastTest/OO_one_event.xml
  (tuned at 200 GeV; EOS 91), and so were the 3dMCGlauber ones until the revision below
  (O16 from nucleusConfigs; tau_form_mean 0.5 until the second revision below), except Subtract_hard_momentum 1 (ISR: the hard
  partons' momentum is taken from the colliding nucleons), generateOnlyPositions 1 for the ISR
  and b <= 3 fm.  (EOS 9 before 2026-10, when iSS could not decay the SMASH list.)

  Revision 2026-11-24, the RHIC bulk tune (analysis/OO-RHIC: oo_bias.py, set g_v045_n215;
  bulk_tune_screening.ipynb).  In this chain (ISR, no UrQMD, iSS at T 0.15) the JETSCAPE MAP
  of 2601.17234 that this file had made too few particles: p+p NSD dN/deta(|eta| < 0.5) 1.74
  against UA5's 2.50, O+O <N_ch> 0.85 of STAR's (central) to 0.50 (60-70 %), d+Au mid-rapidity
  0.84 of PHENIX's (0-20 %).  Minimum-bias screening (10k events per sample, the bulk hadrons
  of iSS) of the MAP, of 2407.17443's p+p set and of 2211.16376's method 3, then a grid around
  2407.17443's set, gave the 3dMCGlauber block below: 2407.17443's p+p set (yloss nodes
  1.6 / 2.15 / 2.15 / 2.15 at y_init 2 / 4 / 6 / 10, shadowing 0.45, BG 5) with the yloss
  variance 0.45 instead of 0.5 (0.5 makes p+p P(N_ch) ~10 % wider than UA5 and the O+O tail
  too long; 0.3 makes it too short).  Changed: ylossParam4At2 1.610 -> 1.6, At4 and At6
  1.685 -> 2.15, At10 2.95 -> 2.15, ylossParam4var 0.682 -> 0.45, shadowing_factor 0 -> 0.45,
  BG 3.96 -> 5.0.  remnant_energy_loss_fraction stays 0.536 (a scan 0.4-1.0 found it the best
  match to PHOBOS's p+p dN/deta shape).  Result (model, not vetted): p+p NSD 2.44 (UA5 2.50),
  P(N_ch) width 1.07 x UA5; O+O <N_ch> 1.01 x STAR with its classes as the top 85.5 % of the
  model's events, p(N_ch) tail (N_ch > 120) 1.04; d+Au mid-rapidity 1.02-1.09 (PHENIX, central),
  1.07 (STAR minimum bias), d-going side ~1.0.  Known misses: the Au-going side of d+Au is 16-57 %
  high (more toward peripheral; not the centrality classes, and shadowing 0.6 / 0.8 or ylossParam4At2
  1.1 do not remove it: the analysis notebook, section 8), and p+p dN/deta is 10-15 % low
  at |eta| 1.5-3 and high beyond 3.5.  Only charged yields and dN/deta were tuned: no <p_T>,
  identified particles or flow; MUSIC is unchanged.  Samples made with this file before
  2026-11-24 (centrality_proxy.py, closure_oo.py) used the MAP block: oo_bias.py's MAP options
  restore it.

  Revision 2026-11-24 (2), the formation time: tau_form_mean 0.5 -> 0.424.  3dMCGlauber's
  tau_form_mean is the effective formation time of this chain (every string decelerates over
  it; MUSIC deposits the strings and, with initial profile 131, overwrites Initial_time_tau_0
  with the earliest string start).  0.424 fm/c is the MAP's tau_form (2601.17234, Table IV: the
  time after which the string energy is deposited) and the value of the Au+Au, Pb+Pb and LHC
  O+O / Ne+Ne XMLs; 0.5 was the default inherited from OO_one_event.xml, with the MAP's 0.424
  only in Initial_time_tau_0.  Checked with the tuned set (oo_bias.py tau0424, same seeds,
  10k events each): p+p NSD dN/deta 2.48 against 2.44 with 0.5, O+O <N_ch> 37.3 against 37.5
  (1.003 x STAR with f 0.860, tail 1.01), d+Au within 1 % (PHENIX 0-20 % Au side / mid / d side
  1.18 / 1.06 / 0.99 of the data, as with 0.5), identified <pT> within 2 % (bulk_tune_screening.ipynb
  sections 9-10).  Changes of 1-2 %, so the bulk parameters above stay; the vacuum chain does not
  depend on it.

  Jet energy loss: Matter above Q0 = 2 GeV and LBT below, Matter with recoils (recoil_on 1),
  the settings of the Au+Au and Pb+Pb jet productions.  LBT's partons and Matter's recoils
  carry the colour flow of every scattering, and the iColored hadronization closes the colour
  lines that end in the medium (<JetHadronization><colour_closure>; X-SCAPE
  lbt_colored_hadro, README_ColourFlow.md).  run_prod_oo_isr.py with its option matter-only
  removes <Lbt> and sets recoil_on 0: Matter alone, the default before 2026-10-21 (when LBT's
  partons had no colour), for builds without the colour closure and to extend Matter-only
  campaigns.

  No hydro reuse: with ISR the medium is made from what each event's hard scattering left,
  so <setReuseHydro> stays false (X-SCAPE refuses true with ISR), also with pTHat windows.

  <nEvents>, <Random><seed>, <Hard><PythiaGun> pTHatMin/pTHatMax/pTHatBins/eCM, <IS><MCGlauber>
  sqrts/b_min/b_max, <slim_bulk_info> and the surface flags are overwritten per job by
  run_prod_oo_isr.py; with its option bulk-hadrons N it appends hadronize.xml's <SoftParticlization>
  (iSS in the job, N oversamples).  See README.md, "Hadronization".
-->

<jetscape>

  <!-- General settings -->
  <nEvents> 10 </nEvents>
  <setReuseHydro> false </setReuseHydro>
  <nReuseHydro> 1 </nReuseHydro>

  <!-- Technical settings -->
  <debug> off </debug>
  <remark> off </remark>
  <vlevel> 0 </vlevel>
  <nEvents_printout> 10 </nEvents_printout>
  <enableAutomaticTaskListDetermination> true </enableAutomaticTaskListDetermination>

  <!--  JetScape Writer Settings: none, run_prod_oo_isr.py writes HDF5 -->
  <outputFilename>prod_OO_isr</outputFilename>
  <JetScapeWriterAscii> off </JetScapeWriterAscii>
  <JetScapeWriterAsciiGZ> off </JetScapeWriterAsciiGZ>
  <JetScapeWriterHepMC> off </JetScapeWriterHepMC>
  <JetScapeWriterRootHepMC> off </JetScapeWriterRootHepMC>
  <JetScapeWriterFinalStatePartonsAscii> off </JetScapeWriterFinalStatePartonsAscii>
  <JetScapeWriterFinalStateHadronsAscii> off </JetScapeWriterFinalStateHadronsAscii>
  <JetScapeWriterQnVectorAscii>off</JetScapeWriterQnVectorAscii>
  <write_centrality> 0 </write_centrality>
  <write_pthat> 0 </write_pthat>

  <Random>
    <seed>1</seed>
  </Random>

  <!-- Initial State Module: must come before <Hard> -->
  <IS>
    <MCGlauber>
      <!--0: generates full event with binary collisions and strings-->
      <!--1: PythiaISR setup (needs 2 step MCGlauber initialization)-->
      <generateOnlyPositions>1</generateOnlyPositions>
      <!--Collision system definitions-->
      <projectile>O</projectile> <!--Projectile name-->
      <target>O</target> <!--Target name-->
      <sqrts>200</sqrts> <!--Center of mass energy in GeV-->
      <!--b selects the centrality inside X-SCAPE (cenMin/cenMax act only in the standalone
          3dMCGlauber). b <= 3 fm is about 0-24% of the O+O cross section (~1.55 b). With ISR
          the nucleon pair of the hard scattering makes no string, so an event whose only
          collision is the hard one may have no medium: keep b small enough.-->
      <b_min>0.0</b_min> <!--Minimum impact parameter in fm-->
      <b_max>3.0</b_max> <!--Maximum impact parameter in fm-->
      <cenMin>0.0</cenMin> <!--Minimum centrality in %  (ignored inside X-SCAPE, see above)-->
      <cenMax>80</cenMax> <!--Maximum centrality in % (ignored inside X-SCAPE, see above)-->
      <nucleon_configuration_from_file>1</nucleon_configuration_from_file> <!--1: O16 configurations from nucleusConfigs (PGCM, with alpha clustering)-->
      <useQuarks>1</useQuarks> <!--Switch to use valence quarks-->
      <Q2>1.0</Q2> <!--Scale when evaluating the PDF-->
      <shadowing_factor>0.45</shadowing_factor> <!--Shadowing factor for producing strings from multiple scatterings (RHIC bulk tune 2026-11-24; MAP 0.0)-->
      <baryon_junctions>0</baryon_junctions> <!--0: baryon number assumed to be at string end, 1: baryon number transported assuming baryon junctions (at smaller x) see arXiv:nucl-th/9602027-->
      <N_sea_partons>1</N_sea_partons> <!--Number of allowed soft partons-->
      <d_min>0.9</d_min> <!--Minimum distance between two nucleons in fm-->
      <lambdaB>0.2</lambdaB> <!--Strength of the baryon junction stopping-->
      <BG>5.0</BG> <!--Gaussian width square for sampling the valence quark positions (GeV^2; RHIC bulk tune 2026-11-24; MAP 3.96)-->
      <!--1 with ISR: the hard partons' momentum is taken from the colliding nucleons
          (valence quark; their remnants go to the jet hadronization, not to strings).
          0 (config/BulkFastTest, no ISR) would count that energy twice.-->
      <Subtract_hard_momentum>1</Subtract_hard_momentum>
      <lambdaBs>0.0</lambdaBs> <!--Fraction of single-to-double junction stopping-->
      <baryonInStringProb>0.0</baryonInStringProb> <!--Relative probility to put a baryon charge in the string rather than at the wounded nucleon remnant-->
      <fluct_Nstrings_per_NN_collision>1</fluct_Nstrings_per_NN_collision> <!--Fluctuate number of strings produced per NN collision-->
      <QCD_string_production_mode>1</QCD_string_production_mode> <!--1: strings are produced randomly in the binary collision list, 2: strings are produced at the last binary collision-->
      <!--Rapidity loss parameters (only mode 4 supported in XML, other modes have to be set in mcglauber.input)-->
      <rapidity_loss_method>4</rapidity_loss_method>
      <!--RHIC bulk tune 2026-11-24 (set g_v045_n215, see the header); MAP: 1.610 / 1.685 /
          1.685 / 2.95, variance 0.682-->
      <ylossParam4At2>1.6</ylossParam4At2>
      <ylossParam4At4>2.15</ylossParam4At4>
      <ylossParam4At6>2.15</ylossParam4At6>
      <ylossParam4At10>2.15</ylossParam4At10>
      <ylossParam4var>0.45</ylossParam4var>
      <remnant_energy_loss_fraction>0.536</remnant_energy_loss_fraction> <!--Nucleon remnant's energy loss fraction (fraction of string's y_loss) [0, 1]-->
      <fluctuation_remnant_energy_loss_fraction>0</fluctuation_remnant_energy_loss_fraction>
      <remnant_energy_loss_fraction_var>0.4</remnant_energy_loss_fraction_var>
      <!--string evolution mode, tau_form = tau_form_mean [fm]-->
      <!--1: deceleration with fixed (90%) rapidity loss (m/sigma = 1 fm, dtau = tau_form)-->
      <!--2: deceleration with LEXUS/parameterized rapidity loss (both dtau and sigma fluctuate)-->
      <!--3: deceleration with LEXUS/parameterized rapidity loss (m/sigma = 1 fm, dtau fluctuates)-->
      <!--4: deceleration with LEXUS/parameterized rapidity loss (dtau = tau_form, m/sigma fluctuates)-->
      <evolve_QCD_string_mode>4</evolve_QCD_string_mode>
      <tau_form_mean>0.424</tau_form_mean> <!--Mean value for tau_form [fm]; the MAP's 0.424 since 2026-11-24 (before 0.5)-->
      <tau_form_fluct_gamma_beta>1.0</tau_form_fluct_gamma_beta> <!--Fluctuation parameter for the gamma distribution-->
    </MCGlauber>

    <!-- MUSIC's grid: +-10.5 fm x +-6 (70 x 70 x 60 cells) since 2026-10-12.  The O+O fireball
         stays within |x|, |y| < 7 fm and the output grid (grid_oo.yaml) within +-9.84 fm; on
         +-10.5 fm the hydro and the freeze-out surface are the same as on +-15 fm to float32
         rounding, with no grid-edge hit in 2,994 events, at +82 % events/h and half the CPU and
         memory per job (docs/BENCHMARK_2x3090.md, "O+O campaign").  For larger b or another
         system check diag/hit_grid_boundary and widen it; the output grid must stay inside. -->
    <grid_max_x> 10.5 </grid_max_x>
    <grid_max_y> 10.5 </grid_max_y>
    <grid_max_z> 6  </grid_max_z>
    <grid_step_x> 0.3 </grid_step_x>
    <grid_step_y> 0.3 </grid_step_y>
    <grid_step_z> 0.2 </grid_step_z>
  </IS>

  <!-- Hard process.  PythiaIsrGun reads the PythiaGun block; <ISR> switches the ISR
       chain on (maxT/deltaT: 0 = the <Eloss> values).  PythiaIsrGun puts the hard
       scattering at a 3dMCGlauber binary collision. -->
  <Hard>
    <PythiaGun>
      <name>PythiaGun</name>
      <FSR_on>0</FSR_on>
      <pTHatMin>20</pTHatMin>
      <pTHatMax>40</pTHatMax>
      <eCM>200</eCM>
      <!-- The RHIC p+p 200 GeV hard tune (analysis/OO-RHIC), at Q0 = 2 and vir_factor 0.25
           (the Matter/LBT settings below): alpha_s(MZ) 0.152 for the hard process and the MPI,
           iMATTER's PDF (NNPDF3.1 NNLO), the tune's MPI (pTmin 5, which Pythia lowers to
           ~1.7 GeV at 200 GeV: ~0.6 MPI per event besides the hard scattering). -->
      <LinesToRead>
        HardQCD:all = on
        PDF:pSet = 20
        SigmaProcess:alphaSvalue = 0.152
        MultipartonInteractions:alphaSvalue = 0.152
        MultipartonInteractions:pTmin = 5.0
      </LinesToRead>
    </PythiaGun>
    <ISR>
      <maxT>0</maxT>
      <deltaT>0</deltaT>
    </ISR>
  </Hard>

  <!--Preequilibrium Dynamics Module: MUSIC builds its string source (InitialProfile 131)
      only with one -->
  <Preequilibrium>
    <tau0>0.0</tau0>
    <taus>0.5</taus>
    <evolutionInMemory>0</evolutionInMemory>
    <NullPreDynamics> </NullPreDynamics>
  </Preequilibrium>

  <!-- Hydro Module -->
  <Hydro>
    <MUSIC>
      <name>MUSIC</name>
      <MUSIC_input_file>music_input</MUSIC_input_file>
      <!--EOS used for the hydro evolution: 91 hotQCD EOS (SMASH list), 9 hotQCD EOS (UrQMD list), 20 NEOS-4D-->
      <!--91, the tuned set's EOS (config/BulkFastTest/OO_one_event.xml): iSS samples the SMASH
          hadron list and decays it itself (hadronize.xml decay_smash_list 1, iSS smash_ready).
          9 (UrQMD list) for reruns of older campaigns: run_prod_oo_isr.py with eos 9-->
      <EOS>91</EOS>
      <!--InitialProfile = 42 for Trento + Pre-equilibrium or IPGlasma, 13 for the 3D Glauber initial condition-->
      <InitialProfile>131</InitialProfile>
      <!--beastMode = 0: double precision, constant time step-->
      <!--beastMode = 1: float precision, constant time step-->
      <!--beastMode = 2: float precision, increased time step after 4 fm/ (can be used for soft sector only runs, otherwise the change in stepsize will lead to errors)-->
      <beastMode>1</beastMode>
      <!--A larger time step from late_tau_switch on (D1, docs/Plans/Final_Optims.md): 0.02 -> 0.05
          fm/c from 3 fm/c, with the freeze-out checks and the stored frames kept at 0.1 fm/c. About
          half the MUSIC steps; the fields change at the level of the time discretization.
          0: a constant step.-->
      <late_delta_tau>0.05</late_delta_tau>
      <late_tau_switch>3.0</late_tau_switch>
      <!--starting time of the hydrodynamic evolution after the pre-equilibrium phase-->
      <Initial_time_tau_0>0.424</Initial_time_tau_0>

      <!--evolution output/storage parameters-->
      <output_evolution_to_file>0</output_evolution_to_file>
      <output_evolution_to_memory>1</output_evolution_to_memory>
      <!--When there is a pre-equilibrium stage, and it is kept in memory, this has to be 1-->
      <!--5 x Delta_Tau (0.02, music_input) = 0.1 fm/c between stored frames = the FNO4d dtau-->
      <output_evolution_every_N_timesteps>5</output_evolution_every_N_timesteps>
      <!-- MUSIC's momentum anisotropy / eccentricity .dat files (four serial passes over
           every cell per run); nothing reads them in production. -->
      <output_momentum_anisotropy_vs_etas>0</output_momentum_anisotropy_vs_etas>
      <surface_in_memory>1</surface_in_memory>
      <!--0: MUSIC fills the framework medium Matter and LBT read (and the hydro file is written from)-->
      <dump_hydro_only>0</dump_hydro_only>
      <!--1: that framework copy keeps e, s, T, vx, vy, vz only (run_prod_oo_isr.py -bulk-info)-->
      <slim_bulk_info>1</slim_bulk_info>
      <!--hand the freeze-out surface to the framework (the particlize file, for iSS offline)-->
      <skip_surface>0</skip_surface>
      <freeze_out_surface>1</freeze_out_surface>

      <!--shear viscosity settings-->
      <shear_viscosity_eta_over_s>0.108</shear_viscosity_eta_over_s>
      <T_dependent_Shear_to_S_ratio>3</T_dependent_Shear_to_S_ratio>
      <!-- Parameters for parametrization 3, the names for these parameters are different compared to JETSCAPE-->
      <shear_viscosity_3_T_kink_in_GeV>0.206</shear_viscosity_3_T_kink_in_GeV>
      <shear_viscosity_3_at_kink>0.108</shear_viscosity_3_at_kink>
      <shear_viscosity_3_low_T_slope_in_GeV>-1.999</shear_viscosity_3_low_T_slope_in_GeV>
      <shear_viscosity_3_high_T_slope_in_GeV>1.999</shear_viscosity_3_high_T_slope_in_GeV>
      <!--mu_B dependent shear viscosity settings-->
      <muB_dependent_Shear_to_S_ratio>0</muB_dependent_Shear_to_S_ratio>
      <!--bulk viscosity settings-->
      <temperature_dependent_bulk_viscosity>3</temperature_dependent_bulk_viscosity>
      <!-- Parameters for parametrization 3, the names for these parameters are different compared to JETSCAPE-->
      <bulk_viscosity_3_max>0.092</bulk_viscosity_3_max>
      <bulk_viscosity_3_T_peak_in_GeV>0.180</bulk_viscosity_3_T_peak_in_GeV>
      <bulk_viscosity_3_width_in_GeV>0.067</bulk_viscosity_3_width_in_GeV>
      <bulk_viscosity_3_lambda_asymm>-0.8</bulk_viscosity_3_lambda_asymm>
      <!--higher order transport coefficients-->
      <Include_second_order_terms>1</Include_second_order_terms>
      <!--Conserved charge settings-->
      <Include_Rhob>0</Include_Rhob>
      <Include_QS>0</Include_QS>
      <!--freeze-out parameters-->
      <!--0: freeze out at freezeout_temperature; eps_switch is then ignored-->
      <use_eps_for_freeze_out>0</use_eps_for_freeze_out>
      <freezeout_temperature>0.15</freezeout_temperature>
      <eps_switch>0.12</eps_switch>
      <Do_FreezeOut_lowtemp>1</Do_FreezeOut_lowtemp>
      <average_surface_over_this_many_time_steps>5</average_surface_over_this_many_time_steps>
      <!--perform CooperFrye Freezout in MUSIC, not needed when iSS module is used-->
      <Perform_CooperFrye_Freezeout>0</Perform_CooperFrye_Freezeout>
      <!--source term parameters for InitialProfile 13-->
      <string_source_sigma_x>0.207</string_source_sigma_x>
      <string_source_sigma_eta>0.458</string_source_sigma_eta>
      <stringPreEqFlowFactor>0.0</stringPreEqFlowFactor>
    </MUSIC>
  </Hydro>

  <!-- Energy loss in MUSIC's medium: Matter before Lbt (Matter sets the virtuality Lbt takes
       over at Q0), <mutex>ON</mutex> arbitrates the handover, as in the Au+Au jet XML.  maxT is
       also the ISR range: iMATTER showers back to -maxT and the final-state shower starts
       there (as in PythiaIsrMUSIC). -->
  <Eloss>
    <!-- <nThreads> -1 </nThreads>: the showers of an event in parallel (OpenMP), as many
         threads as OMP_NUM_THREADS; X-SCAPE's main XML documents it (its default: 0,
         serial).  Not set here: run_prod_oo_isr.py puts -1 in by default (0 on an X-SCAPE
         without the setting) and records what the job ran with; its eloss-threads option
         changes it (0: serial), and a value set here wins over the driver's default.
         Changes the events (own random streams per shower): one setting per campaign. -->
    <deltaT> 0.1 </deltaT>
    <maxT> 50 </maxT>
    <!-- With a hydro (MUSIC) Matter and LBT replace tStart by the hydro's start time,
         MUSIC's tau0 of the run (X-SCAPE tstart_hydro_tau0): the medium interaction begins
         with the stored evolution, before it the lookup is vacuum.  This value applies only
         without a hydro. -->
    <tStart> 0.5 </tStart>
    <mutex> ON </mutex>
    <Matter>
      <name> Matter </name>
      <matter_on> 1 </matter_on>
      <Q0> 2.0 </Q0>
      <in_vac> 0 </in_vac>
      <!-- the start time (MUSIC's tau0) at each point's own proper time, i.e. the events
           of tStart 0 with MUSIC's lookup deciding (X-SCAPE 2026-10-28; default 0) -->
      <tStart_at_point> 1 </tStart_at_point>
      <vir_factor> 0.25 </vir_factor>
      <!-- 1: recoils and holes (pstat -1), with their colour (not hadronized; iColored
           closes the colour lines they leave open) -->
      <recoil_on> 1 </recoil_on>
      <broadening_on> 0 </broadening_on>
      <brick_med> 0 </brick_med>
      <hydro_Tc> 0.16 </hydro_Tc>
      <qhat0> -2.0 </qhat0>
      <alphas> 0.25 </alphas>
      <QhatParametrizationType> 1 </QhatParametrizationType>
    </Matter>
    <Lbt>
      <name> Lbt </name>
      <Q0> 2.0 </Q0>
      <in_vac> 0 </in_vac>
      <only_leading> 0 </only_leading>
      <hydro_Tc> 0.16 </hydro_Tc>
      <alphas> 0.25 </alphas>
      <run_alphas> 1 </run_alphas>
    </Lbt>
  </Eloss>

  <!-- Jet hadronization: the final partons and the beam remnants through the ISR colour
       flow.  Needs the live event (remnants from 3dMCGlauber), so it runs in the job.
       <colour_closure>: how the colour lines that end in the medium (the holes of LBT and
       of Matter's recoils) are closed: reconnect (join the open ends within a shower, the
       holes' medium partners for the rest), reconnect_global, thermal, fake, none
       (prod_OO_isr/README.md, X-SCAPE README_ColourFlow.md). -->
  <JetHadronization>
    <name>iColored</name>
    <colour_closure>reconnect</colour_closure>
  </JetHadronization>

</jetscape>
